# Files the Vercel CLI must not upload when deploying from a checkout.
#
# Patterns are ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored name matches a directory
# of that name ANYWHERE in the tree: `backups` silently excluded the admin route
# src/app/[locale]/(app)/admin/backups/ from every Vercel build, so
# /en/admin/backups answered 404 in production while a local `next build`
# (which never consults this file) served it fine. `.gitignore` had the same
# unanchored rule and the same effect on the committed tree.
#
# Rule of thumb: root-anchor anything that names a project-root directory;
# leave genuinely ubiquitous directories (node_modules, coverage) unanchored.

# Dependencies & build artifacts
node_modules
/.next
/out
/build

# Data & backups
/.data
/backups
/freebuff

# Dev/cache
/.freebuff
/.vercel
coverage
/test-results
/playwright-report

# Scratch — isolated dist dirs and repro copies live here (gitignored, and
# routinely ~1.5GB: a CLI `vercel --prod` was uploading the lot before it
# aborted). CI deploys a clean checkout, but the local CLI path needs this.
/tmp

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Git
/.git
/.github

# Documentation (except README)
/docs
*.md
!README.md

# OS
.DS_Store
